-- Creature sizes from the VMaNGOS import were applied twice. VMaNGOS display_scale is the creature's whole size (0 = use the
-- model's own size), and the 1.12 client used it instead of the model scale. The 1.60 client multiplies DisplayScale with
-- CreatureDisplayInfo.CreatureModelScale, so the import's copy of the VMaNGOS value shrank or grew the creature a second time:
-- Duskbat 0.4 x model 0.4 = 0.16 (players: "much smaller than live"). Live sniffs agree: every vanilla creature seen on the
-- live realm has DisplayScale 1 with the size in the model, e.g. Burly Rockjaw Trogg 705 = 0.7 on live = VMaNGOS 0.7.
-- Fix: DisplayScale = VMaNGOS size / client model scale, for the 158 rows where the import copied an explicit VMaNGOS size onto
-- a model whose own scale is not 1 (rows on models of scale 1 were already right). Each row only changes while it still holds
-- the imported value, so later sniff or hand fixes (Warpwood Crusher 13021) stay.
UPDATE `creature_template_model` SET `DisplayScale` = 0.99 WHERE `CreatureID` = 69 AND `Idx` = 0 AND `CreatureDisplayID` = 604 AND ABS(`DisplayScale` - 0.7) < 0.001; -- 0.7 / 0.71
